Found the root cause. The Return SV is pushed into `cond_uses`. So at fold time, when stmt 0 defines `r8 v0` and `r8 v0` is in `cond_uses` (because it's returned) but has no `sv_consumer_stmt` entry (returns aren't statements with inputs), it hits `decision=cond-only` and gets folded.

This `cond_uses` overload for returns is intentional for some single-return-folding cases, but it breaks the multi-branch merge case. The cleanest fix: track returned SVs separately and block folding when the output is returned AND defined in a branch (depth > 0) — or more simply, when the returned value has multiple definitions across branches.

